---
// The page opens on the visitor's problem, not on the product. Everything below
// this section is an answer to one of these three, in the same order.
//
// No dollar figures here on purpose: the honest ones depend on their volume and
// their per-guest price, and a number that collapses under one question does
// more damage than no number. The arithmetic belongs on the call, where the
// inputs are theirs.
const failures = [
	{
		tag: 'TUESDAY, LATE',
		title: 'The math is done by hand, every time',
		body: 'Scale every recipe to the count. Add up the same herb across four dishes. Write the shopping list, then the prep sheet. Then the client moves 180 to 240 on Thursday and you do it again.'
	},
	{
		tag: 'THE REAL NUMBER',
		title: 'And the cost at the end is a guess',
		body: 'The recipe says five pounds of peeled shallots. The case you buy has the skins on. Almost nobody charges the trim, so the plate costs more than the sheet says, on every dish with something to peel.'
	},
	{
		tag: 'THE SPREADSHEET',
		title: 'The thing holding it together is fragile',
		body: 'One person built it. Somebody broke a formula last spring. The caper-lemon butter is written out in three places, so fixing it once fixes one third of the problem.'
	}
];
---

<section id="problem" class="container-page border-t border-hairline py-section-tight">
	<div class="max-w-2xl" data-reveal>
		<p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
		<h2 class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">Every order is a night of arithmetic.</h2>
		<!-- One sentence tying these three back to the headline. The h1 names the
		     quote call; these cards are the workload, which is the symptom, and
		     without this line the fold and the section below it read as two
		     separate pitches stapled together. -->
		<p class="mt-5 text-lede text-ink-soft">
			Not the cooking. The part before it, and the part nobody trained for: turning a menu
			and a headcount into what to buy, what to make, and what it costs. It is also why
			the number you gave on the phone was a guess. Nothing here is finished in time to
			have told you.
		</p>
	</div>

	<ul role="list" class="mt-12 grid gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-x-12 lg:gap-y-0">
		{
			failures.map((item, i) => (
				<li
					class="border-t border-hairline-strong pt-6"
					data-reveal
					style={`--reveal-delay: ${i * 90}ms`}
				>
					<p class="font-mono text-eyebrow font-semibold tracking-wide text-amber-deep">
						{item.tag}
					</p>
					<h3 class="mt-3 text-h3 font-semibold">{item.title}</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">{item.body}</p>
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ul>
</section>
